(footprint "R_LapPad_T50R0-250-12X"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "aiee-librarian")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Vishay/Barry T50R0-250-12X, 50 ohm 250W BeO flanged RF termination. RESISTOR BODY IS OFF-BOARD, bolted to the user's external heatsink beside the PCB - only the RF tab (3.048 x 0.127 mm, silver-plated copper) laps onto this ONE SMD pad. Pad 1 = RF. There is no second electrical pad on the board: the resistor's cold end returns through its flange to the heatsink, NOT through the PCB - PCB GND and the resistor's cold end meet ONLY AT THE HEATSINK. Pad sized 5.0 x 7.0 mm (tab is 3.048 mm wide) for a hand-solder lap overlap of ~4-6mm carrying 1.732 Arms continuous (150W/50ohm CW) - deliberately generous. The off-board mechanical envelope (flange 24.77x9.525mm, 2x Dia 3.302mm mounting holes 18.42mm apart on the flange centreline 3.175mm from each end, body block 9.525x9.525mm centred, tab exiting the middle of one 24.77mm side) is documented on User.Drawings ONLY, as a heatsink drilling template - ORIGIN (0,0) = the point where the tab centreline crosses the board edge; local +Y = into the board, -Y = off-board toward the resistor/heatsink. The flange-to-board-edge GAP drawn there (1.0mm) is ILLUSTRATIVE ONLY - the true X-Y offset from the board edge is an outline/placement decision (architect's, not this footprint's). Courtyard is PAD-ONLY (+0.25mm margin), deliberately NOT wrapped around the off-board body: LEARNINGS 2026-07-22 - an off-board courtyard on a declared-edge part generates false placement-legality failures; keeping courtyard on-board avoids the argument entirely. Silk registration marks at the board edge show the flange/tab centreline (local X=0) and the two bolt centrelines (local X=+/-9.21mm) so a builder can align the physical part to the pad. BeO SUBSTRATE HAZARD: beryllium oxide ceramic, sealed/covered element, safe under normal mounting - DO NOT machine, drill, grind or crush the resistor body (toxic dust).")
	(tags "RF termination flange lap-pad off-board BeO heatsink")
